{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/533710-re-running-trinity","id":533710,"title":"Re-running Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-30T15:52:17-07:00","id":533710,"title":"Re-running Trinity","content":"So, here's the deal. I have a very long-running gaming group. Some people have been gaming with me for 17 years. Others less than 2. So, it's an eclectic mix. <br /> <br /> About 1/3 of my players have played Trinity before, some of them twice, in multi-year campaigns. They talk about these old games with fondness and now the 2/3 of my players who have not played Trinity before are asking about it. I'm glad they're interested in it, but I'm wondering how to shake things up a little so that it wouldn't seem quite as much of a repeat to those who have played Trinity once or twice before. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5930-deathchipmunk","name":"DeathChipmunk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:29:32-07:00","id":533754,"title":"","content":"The <b>Trinity</b> Universe and the forthcoming <b>Trinity</b> Continuum feature a lots of genres and tones across the length and breadth of the settings. The 2120s of <b>Trinity</b> alone contains optimistic space opera explorers, transhuman utopias and cyberpunk dystopias, post-apocalypse wastelands, military SF with mutated monsters on ruined colony planets and more. While a multi-year series might cover a lot of ground, there could still be areas you and your players haven't touched on.<br /> <br /> Shifting to another genre within the setting can have a big effect, for one thing. A 'classic' <b>Trinity</b> game featuring a Proteus team of troubleshooters from the Psion Orders, undertaking dangerous missions in various parts of the setting, could be action-heavy or more about subtle espionage and investigation.<br /> <br /> As a personal example of that, I've run that 'classic' game but I've also done military SF on KLG (and used the rules for a different military SF game) and planned for a series about deep space exploration and recontacting extrasolar colonies influenced by &quot;starship shows&quot; like <b>Star Trek</b>, which I discussed at length in the 'Creating a Story' chapter of the fan-written <a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook/Introduction\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Storytellers Handbook</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T22:52:44-07:00","id":534063,"title":"","content":"I'll agree with Oxbrow again here, i've personally run Darkness Revealed three different ways and that's a pretty strict genre-piece for the most part. With free-reign you can take the setting anywhere the players want to go with it.<br /> If there's a particular revelation that you would like to reinvent then specify it. The reconnection with the Extrasolar Colonies? Huang-Marr? The Chromatic Invasion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}